{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/487924-conspiracy-the-dead-musicians","id":487924,"title":"[Conspiracy] The Dead Musicians","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-21T20:58:08-07:00","id":487924,"title":"[Conspiracy] The Dead Musicians","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Dead Musicians</span></div> <br /> To understand the Dead Musicians, you have to understand Anita Dietrich, their founder. A flute instructor in Stuttgart back in the 1920s, she was a quiet and reserved woman, not one for parties or public life. Her life would have gone on as it did, boring and private, if the music hadn't started playing for her.<br /> It started one Tuesday night; she had gotten up to go to the bathroom when she heard the pounding of drums. After a scant few minutes, an entire orchestra had joined in, playing a sweet and alien music that left her tapping her feet. After a few minutes it quieted down again, and she went to sleep. It was only the next morning when she found out that her neighbor had passed away the night before.<br /> This happened again and again over the next few weeks; she would hear snatches of wonderful music, and would discover that someone had died soon thereafter. She would have gone on believing it was just a curiosity if not for her cousin's murder.<br /> The music started, just like it had a dozen times before; however, the instruments sounded ill-tuned, and they screeched and yowled through her head, screeching out her cousin's name. By the time she had reached the room, he was dead, strangled by a tablecloth; the murderer had left through the window.<br /> The police were baffled; she, however, could <i>hear</i> where the killer was, like a broken orchestra heard far away. She tracked him down, and left an anonymous note with the police; they found evidence of several murders in his home, and he was sentenced to a life in prison.<br /> And so a pattern emerged; she would hear a murder (or a murderer), and would track them down. At the same time, she could hear the motifs laced through-out the music of others; some discrete questions led to her discovering that she wasn't the only one. She started gathering together a group of vigilantes as the police were less and less able to maintain order - in the last days of the Weimar Republic, their &quot;hobby&quot; and their professional lives grew closer together. If you go back and look at sheet music of the era, these <i>Totentanzer</i> had begun writing songs laced with the motifs of their nightly vigil.<br /> At first, the rise of the Third Reich was seen as a return to order; Kristallnacht disabused them of this notion. They remained in Germany for only a few more months before they fled, first to France and then to countries further afield; the movement was broken up before it could get started.<br /> The history of the next 50 years is patchy; the members took up careers, gave lessons, and generally lived and died. Each one, however, ended up finding others like them, forming tiny &quot;quartets&quot; of vigilante musicians; some of them even stumbled into the Supernatural, joining Hunter cells where their strange gift was appreciated (if a little suspect).<br /> Of course, if they had stayed little islands of music, the Dead Musicians wouldn't exist; however, in 1985, a student of one of the original <i>Totentanzer</i> secured a record deal.<br /> The resulting flurry of mail led to a meet-up in Detroit, where the different groups swapped tips and tricks, and the less Supernatural-savvy attendees were filled in about ghosts and other undead. Some of the members that showed up weren't themselves musicians; they heard and recognized the motifs and melodies, even if they couldn't replicate them themselves.<br /> This meet-up happened again in 1988 and 1991; after that point, the different groups coalesced into what is now known as the Dead Musicians. No one's <i>exactly</i> sure what brought this about, though some people point to a trip made in 1993 to Germany, where members visited former concentration camps - after all, it would take an orchestra to placate that many ghosts.<br /> <br /> <b>The Enemy</b><br /> The Dead Musicians primarily concern themselves with ghosts and Slashers; the first they help move on, and the second they... dispatch. Of course, they don't overlook other denizens of the night; while their talents extend mostly to the dead, the undead certainly come to their attention. Some of the more cynical members point out that they aren't exactly doing this out of the goodness of their heart; when being within a block of the walking dead fills your head with shrieking discord, you oftentimes end up laying them to rest just to get some peace and quiet.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunters</b><br /> Like a lot of kids, you were sent to piano lessons; unlike a lot of kids, your instructor explained why you got music stuck in your head, as well as why it sounded like garbage. After you got old enough, she dragged you on a monster hunting expedition, and here you are.<br /> <br /> &lt;Two more, one of which is &quot;non-typical&quot;&gt;<br /> <br /> <b>Attitudes</b><br /> &lt;I dunno; ideally, they should all get an Expression speciality. For thematic reasons.&gt;<br /> <br /> <b>Status</b><br /> The Dead Musicians still meet up in Detroit every so often, to swap secrets and generally keep in touch. While they are otherwise decentralized, some members do have more respect than others.<br /> <br /> \u2022: You've just been inducted by the Dead Musicians; while you might have been hearing the <i>Totentanz</i> for a while now, you're just starting to learn how to <i>play</i> it. You may purchase dots in <i>Totentanz</i> Stanzas.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022: You've been playing for a while; you've helped a few ghosts and might have even helped take down a Slasher or two. You've heard a few things, too; you receive two Contacts, one in the Dead Musicians and one in the Twilight Network (G:tSE 87).<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022: At this point, the only people more respected than you are the surviving founders - or the ghosts of the dead ones. As such, the Musicians have your back; you gain Allies (The Dead Musicians) at three dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T20:59:35-07:00","id":487941,"title":"","content":"<i>Reserved for the Endowment.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T21:00:21-07:00","id":487943,"title":"","content":"<i>Reserved for Stereotypes</i>.<br /> <br /> Ideas? I need ideas for &quot;starting characters&quot; and Attitudes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T02:33:50-07:00","id":489191,"title":"","content":"They are a really interesting group, and the connection between art and death was always an appealing one IMO.. Are their endowments are more about allowing ghosts to move on, or that they have some darker abilities, like enslaving the dead with a dark song and forcing them to dance to their own will? Also, how does their abilities interact with the more physical undead (zombies, vampires, mummies, etc)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T08:58:59-07:00","id":489552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the same time, she could hear the motifs laced through-out the music of others; some discrete questions led to her discovering that she wasn't the only one. </div> </div> </div>This raises an interesting question. Anita Dietrich could have had an Unseen Sense for death, and a psychic gift for sniffing out murder, both manifesting as music. But when many others have similar abilities manifesting in the same music, that suggests it comes from an outside source. The most obvious answer to that would be some sort of entity picking people to send the music to. But a better angle is probably the music being like a force that some people are susceptible to - once they hear it from somewhere, like a Musician's performance, they can hear it at work in the world and learn to use it - even then though, it suggests the Musicians are internally supernaturally different from other people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Dead Musicians primarily concern themselves with ghosts and Slashers; the first they help move on, and the second they... dispatch. </div> </div> </div>What do they think of Sineaters? The reason I ask is that whatever the Endowment turns out to be - and wherever it comes from - it probably counts as enough of a supernatural connection to death to qualify a Musician for the Bargain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &lt;Two more, one of which is &quot;non-typical&quot;&gt; </div> </div> </div>You're a professional landscape gardener. You've always felt a comforting sense from plants, the ongoing growth and decay surrounding you. One day, you heard a street busker playing the music you used to hum while working - the subsequent conversation told you a lot more about that music and what it means. It's still all about life and death, growth and decay, and the garden is still where you feel whole, but you're pulling things a lot more dangerous than weeds now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &lt;I dunno; ideally, they should all get an Expression speciality. For thematic reasons.&gt; </div> </div> </div>My first thought is one specialising in remembrances - supernaturally speaking, they specialise in ghosts - but also funerals, wakes, vigils for the dead, the dying, and the maybe soon to die. One that believes the Music is worthwhile force in its own right - fighting evils and looking after victims is good and worth doing, but their real faith stretches further, into trying to spread the Music to more and more listeners. The next most obvious third would be one focussing on killers, but I can't think of anything to expand on it. But I could also see a faction who, rather than trust in the Music, try to understand it, and study other beings and magics associated with death to understand the Music's greater place in the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reserved for Stereotypes. </div> </div> </div>The Loyalists come from the same time and place as the Musicians; the Musicians may be among the few who know who the Loyalists are. If you go with the idea of the Musicians being innately supernatural, then the Lucifuge are a good comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T03:17:01-07:00","id":492480,"title":"","content":"Slashers have been known to come back as revenants, so the dead musicians might be known to have to dispatch of a slasher twice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}